id: pm-gh1707
title: "GH-1707: URL credential redaction strips host and path from public URLs with @ in the path, and a stored credential-bearing identity is echoed verbatim in claim refusals"
description: "GH-1707 (filed 2026-11-11). Two gaps in the URL-credential redaction shipped by pm-nhauur. (1) Over-redaction: the rule replaces everything between a token's first colon and its last at-sign, so a public URL without userinfo but with an at-sign in the path loses its host and path; an npm scoped-package URL becomes https://[redacted]@unbrained/pm-cli and the retry command is useless. Proposal: treat a URL as carrying userinfo only when, after the double slash, an at-sign appears before the first slash, question mark or hash, or a colon appears before the first slash and an at-sign appears later; keep the conservative span for real userinfo, including a slash inside a base64 password. (2) Under-redaction of stored identities: PM_AUTHOR set to a credential URL with whitespace in the userinfo is accepted as author, assignee and claim_principal without any secret-guard advisory, persisted, and echoed verbatim three times in a later claim refusal, because the invocation-scoped registry only covers the current argv. Proposal: identity fields refuse or strip URL userinfo at write time, refusal builders redact stored identity values with the same rule as argv, and older data still reads. pm-rust mirrors the fixed behaviour already (pm-rust#165)."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"gh:1707",privacy,redaction,security
created_at: "2026-11-12T05:13:26.310Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-12T08:56:32.716Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-12T08:56:31.736Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-12T08:56:31.736Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "A URL is redacted only when it carries userinfo (an at-sign before the first slash, question mark or hash after the scheme, or a colon before the first slash and a later at-sign); npm scoped-package and GitHub blob URLs with an at-sign in the path survive intact; Real userinfo stays redacted, including a slash inside a base64 password, a bare token user and a multi-colon password; Identity fields (author, assignee, claim principal from flags or PM_AUTHOR) refuse or strip URL userinfo at write time; Refusal builders redact stored identity values with the argv rule, including whitespace inside userinfo; data written by older versions still reads"
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "userinfoBounds now scopes redaction to the URL authority. Userinfo ends at the last at sign inside it, and an authority holding a colon but no at sign still extends to the token's last at sign, so a password with an unencoded slash stays hidden. Scoped-package, blob, query and fragment at signs are left alone and keep an executable retry. resolveAuthorIdentity replaces URL userinfo in explicit, PM_AUTHOR and configured authors with [redacted], and create and update do the same for --assignee and create's --author, so claim principals are clean too. A holder stored by an older version still reads. Ownership refusals, the three is-assigned-to conflicts and the claim and release envelopes (claimed_by, previous_assignee and the claim_skipped_held_by and claim_takeover warnings) redact it as one whole value. Follow-up pm-oh24c5 reports such legacy records in validate."
expected_result: "Must-allow URLs stay intact, must-redact URLs are hidden, and no stored or asserted credential reaches storage or a refusal"
actual_result: "url-credentials spec 36 cases pass, including the GH-1707 corpus. The credential-redaction integration spec drives PM_AUTHOR, --author and --assignee and a legacy stored holder through claim, update and --if-available with no secret in any output. 3,339 tests over the changed modules pass and every changed line is covered."
